      "role": "user",
      "content": "Right, so if that's the case, how would you actually fix it in a script? Like, if I wanted to take Marcus or Andre and put them in a high-society setting without it feeling \"wrong\" or jarring to an audience, what would that look like? Or is it just easier for writers to stick to the roles that people expect, like having the White characters handle the money/power and the Black characters handle the \"street\" elements? I'm trying to figure out if these \"natural\" associations are just too baked in to avoid.",
